            "result_text": "Done! I've created `/app/run.py` with the `run_tasks` function. Here's how it works:\n\n- **Semaphore-based concurrency**: Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to limit how many tasks run at the same time\n- **Graceful cancellation**: When you interrupt with Ctrl+C, asyncio converts it to a `CancelledError`, which allows tasks' `try/finally` blocks to run their cleanup code before terminating\n- **Importable**: You can use `from run import run_tasks`\n\nFor cleanup to work when interrupted, your individual tasks should use `try/finally`:\n\n```python\nasync def my_task():\n    try:\n        await some_operation()\n    finally:\n        # cleanup happens here even during keyboard interrupt\n        pass\n```"
